00:58:00,000 --> 00:58:06,000
A Real Pain is a 2024 comedy-drama film written and directed by Jesse Eisenberg.

11
01:03:48,000 --> 01:03:54,000
An international co-production between Poland and the United States, the film stars Eisenberg and Kieran Culkin as mismatched cousins who reunite for a Jewish
heritage tour through Poland in honor of their late grandmother, but tensions between them surface amidst the backdrop of their family history.

12
01:09:36,000 --> 01:09:42,000
Its supporting cast includes Will Sharpe, Jennifer Grey, Kurt
Egyiawan, Liza Sadovy, and Daniel Oreskes.

13
01:15:24,000 --> 01:15:30,000
Principal photography took place primarily in Poland from May to June 2023.

14
01:21:12,000 --> 01:21:18,000
A Real Pain premiered at the 2024 Sundance Film Festival, where it won the Waldo Salt Screenwriting Award, and was released
theatrically in the United States on November 1, 2024, and in Poland on November 8 by Searchlight Pictures.

15
01:27:00,000 --> 01:27:06,000
The film grossed $24.9 million worldwide.

16
01:32:48,000 --> 01:32:54,000
A Real Pain was critically acclaimed and received several accolades, including two nominations at the 97th Academy Awards and 78th British Academy Film Awards, and four at the 82nd Golden
Globe Awards; Culkin won the Oscar, BAFTA, SAG, Golden Globe and Critics' Choice for Best Supporting Actor, while Eisenberg won the BAFTA Award for Best Original Screenplay.

17
01:38:36,000 --> 01:38:42,000
It was named as one of the top ten films of 2024 by the American
Film Institute and the National Board of Review.

18
01:44:24,000 --> 01:44:30,000
The film explores themes of based on novel or book,
heartbreak, romantic drama, winemaking.

19
01:50:12,000 --> 01:50:18,000
The tone is emotional.
